Notice that we can arrange the sequence like so:

$$
\begin{aligned}
1-\frac12-\frac14+\frac18-\frac{1}{16}-\frac{1}{32}+\frac{1}{64}-\frac{1}{128}-\cdots  &= 1-\frac{5}{8}-\frac{5}{64}-\frac{5}{512}-\dots \\ &= 1-\left(\sum_{i=1}^{\infty}\frac{5}{8^n}\right) \\ &= 1-\frac{5}{7} \text{ (by the convergence of a geometric series)} \\ &=\frac{2}{7}
\end{aligned}
$$

hence our answer is $\boxed{B}$
